# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025766> (Abnormal affect)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:37925091") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025766> "An anomaly in intensity, frequency, or duration of the verbal or behavioral expression of emotions, feelings, or thoughts.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025766> "2024-07-21T12:00:05Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025766> "Affect includes a combination of emotion in terms of feelings and its expression either in the verbal or behavioral (action) level. Normal expressions are often relatively short lived and familiar to the person while pathological expressions may be intense and extended and considered out of character for the individual. Affect encompasses: 1) emotions, 2) volition, and 3) what is termed the intellect or cognitive elements expressing (communicating) emotion and volition. Affect includes an internal feeling (emotion), an internal drive (will), and a motor component expression (typically speech, but also reflected in thoughts).")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025766> "Abnormal affect")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025766> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0011446>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025769> (Disordered formal thought process)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:30416391") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:31582814") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025769> "An abnormality in the dynamic mode, rate, or form of thought processes as recognized from the flow of ideas expressed in speech. Successive thoughts and speech are easily diverted by external stimuli or internal superficial associations. Unable to maintain a constant train of thought and loose themselves in side issues, losing the thread and are unable to recover it. Superficial connections appear to drive the subject matter.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025769> "2024-07-21T12:48:31Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasAlternativeId> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025769> "HP:5200235")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasSynonymType> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/hp#plural_form>) <http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025769> "Disordered formal thought processes")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025769> "Formal thought disorder")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025769> "Disorganized speech or communication")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025769> "Disordered thinking patterns and cognitive processes that are expressed in speech. Expressed speech reflects disorganized thoughts and may include idiosyncratic use of words with illogical meanings, disjointed or fragmented sentence structure that makes it difficult to follow the logic of statements. Also included are abnormalities in rate or speed, and intensity of thoughts as reflected in variations in rate and volume of expressed speech.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025769> "Disordered formal thought process")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025769> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025792>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025779> (Disorder of thought content)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "PMID:36425242") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025779> "Thought content disorders are characterized by abnormal beliefs and convictions (that are to be assessed given the culture and personal background of the affected individual).")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025779> "2024-07-21T15:29:08Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasAlternativeId> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025779> "HP:5200269")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasExactSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025779> "Abnormal thought pattern")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025779> "Thought content disorders are determined by evaluating the meanings of thoughts. The most prominent thought content disorder seen in schizophrenia is delusions. There are overvalued thoughts at some point between normal thinking and delusion. Obsessions, mystical and metaphysical thoughts also reflect abnormal thought content.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025779> "Disorder of thought content")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025779> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025792>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025780> (Abnormal volitional state)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025780> "An abnormality of internal states of motivation or drive that compromise, or interfere with, the ability of the person to attend to basic personal, social, or vocational activities.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025780> "2024-07-21T16:05:20Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasAlternativeId> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025780> "HP:5200275")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025780> "Abnormal energy")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasRelatedSynonym> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025780> "Abnormal motivation")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025780> "Abnormal volitional state")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025780> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025766>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025783> (Diagnostic behavioral phenotype)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025783> "The Human Phenotype Ontology provides terms to describe specific phenotypic abnormalities rather than disease diagnoses. Nevertheless, it is common for descriptions such as 'Autism' to be used to describe individuals affected with Mendelian forms of neurodevelopmental disease and many other conditions. If possible, we recommend annotation using specific terms in other branchs of the Atypical behavior subontology, but if this is not possible, then terms from this branch may be used.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025783> "2024-08-03T10:05:59Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025783> "Diagnostic behavioral phenotype")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025783> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0000708>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025785> (Abnormal preoccupation)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025785> "Preoccupations refers to being absorbed in any particular thought, activity, or concern that captures the attention of the individual. It may have a positive or negative connotation.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025785> "2024-08-03T10:19:52Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025785> "Abnormal preoccupation")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025785> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025779>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025792> (Abnormal cognitive process)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025792> "An abnormal cognitive process can be defined as a deviation from the typical development, structural organization, or functional execution of mental operations that connect informational inputs to behavioral outputs, typically involve at least one of the following processes: perception, memory, learning, emotion, intentionality, self-representation, rationality, and decision-making.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025792> "2024-08-07T17:25:08Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025792> "Definition adapted from Newen A (2017) What are cognitive processes? An example-based approach. Synthese 194:4251-4268.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025792> "Abnormal cognitive process")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025792> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0011446>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025798> (Abnormal wrist morphology)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025798> "Any structural anomaly of the wrist.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025798> "2025-03-01T12:11:21Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025798> "Abnormal wrist morphology")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025798> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0003019>)

# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025799> (Abnormal wrist physiology)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025799> "Any functional anomaly of the wrist.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025799> "2025-03-01T12:12:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025799> "Abnormal wrist physiology")
SubClassOf(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0025799> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0003019>)


)